+# RMI4 touch producer (opt-in)
+
+This Redox process scans F01/F12, uses an explicitly supplied F12 Data1 offset and slot count, and forwards the first finger to `inputd` as pointer movement and left-button state. Example syntax is `rmi4d OFFSET SLOTS`; run only after oracle capture validates both values and the bus/rails/clocks. It polls every 16 ms because TLMM IRQ 125 is not yet wired through the current driver. It is not enabled in initfs. The process exits on I2C errors and releases any held button. Run host tests in `../rmi4-touch-core`; the Redox target build and hardware event path remain unverified.
